  "change": "The existing artifact runner accepts an explicit Python/R language; the common publication entry dispatches that frozen language through its existing executor. R reads transported JSON with jsonlite and can inspect captured RDS/RData bytes natively. No new runtime, scheduler, converter, statistical rule, source repair or automatic backend fallback. Net production growth is three lines; no module is added.",
  "verification_scope": "A fresh opaque compressed RDS contains labels, matrix dimnames, a factor, typed NA, NaN, Inf and raw bytes. Native empirical/source-replication checks preserve these, CRLF report, missing inventory and seed/count. Corrupt/missing files fail; a deliberately nonmatching expectation fails its check without altering the input. Large candidates remain data, not embedded source. Invalid language/profile rejects; unavailable webR jsonlite reports its original dependency failure, never native fallback. No actual published file, method, theorem or mathematical verdict is tested.",
  "limits": "Exact method-specific parser/coordinate maps, numerical tolerances, reference interpretation, confirmatory precision, independent assessment, actual matched study conditions and prospective freeze are unfinished. Native RData parsing is available for a separately qualified evaluator; this fixture checks RDS, not author RData objects or saved closures. Legacy callers retain their Python default and no consumed result is rerun or rescored.",
  "revisions": "The first uncommitted full run was stopped after the package line-budget assertion failed at 150007 lines. The same source generator was consolidated from repeated string concatenation into readable templates; the existing 150000 bound was unchanged. Final package total is 149999. Early fixture correction explicitly disables unused optional dimensions and tests the actually available native-jsonlite profile; unavailable webR remains a negative case, not a weakened positive check.",
